# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the fuzz and ASan jobs (.github/workflows/fuzz.yml), passed with
# LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<path to this file>.
#
# Property slots and array elements hold values NaN-boxed (`PackedValue` in
# crates/lumen/src/value.rs): a string, symbol or BigInt handle is stored with a tag in the top
# 16 bits. LeakSanitizer only recognises plain addresses, so a handle referenced only from a
# packed slot looks unreachable and is reported as a direct leak while the engine still holds it.
# Objects live in GC chunks that stay reachable, so these three allocators are the only ones
# affected. Rc-cycle leaks of objects are counted by the realm-cleanup tests instead.
leak:lumen::lstr::LStr
leak:lumen::value::SymbolData
leak:lumen_common::bigint::BigIntData
